<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuelan heavy oil venture goes to Congress Thur.</title>
<headline>Venezuelan heavy oil venture goes to Congress Thur.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuela's Minister of Energy and Mines Erwin Arrieta is due in Congress on Thursday to present a joint-venture between state oil subsidiary Lagoven, Mobil and Veba, a ministry spokeswoman said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The presentation is a prelude to congressional approval of the $2.6 billion project which aims to produce 120,000 barrels per day of heavy crude from the Cerro Negro area of the Orinoco Oil Belt. The project was originally due to be presented to Congress on February 28, but was delayed.</p>
<p>((-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
